WEBVTT

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:39.060
I've come to get you.

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:41.680
What?

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:44.980
No wake-up kiss?

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:53.400
It's why I'm going to live in this town

00:00:54.110 --> 00:01:00.580
I'm watching an endless dream

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:07.040
Aren't you watching too?

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:14.380
It's always close by no matter how far away it seems

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:21.220
Can't you see it too?

00:01:22.970 --> 00:01:26.640
The things you can't normally say

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:29.400
The things you try to express

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:31.900
The things you're willing to fight for

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:37.610
Standing on your own two feet

00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:44.290
The night sky illuminates them all

00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:51.420
The first flash of lightning

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:57.760
This is our battle to fight

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:05.100
It's why I'm going to live in this town

00:02:05.390 --> 00:02:13.570
This dream will absolutely come true

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:26.330
Where's Hana?

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:30.630
You got her out safely, then.

00:02:32.130 --> 00:02:33.040
Of course.

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:36.170
I'm relieved.

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:40.390
I'm no longer one of the Planetary Gears,

00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:42.100
so I don't think I can go inside the <i>Blume</i>.

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:45.060
Nice work, Captain.

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:53.400
The Midsummer's Knights are to gather
in the briefing room in thirty minutes.

00:02:56.190 --> 00:02:57.110
Roger.

00:02:59.030 --> 00:03:00.610
Wow...

00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:02.370
I've never seen them in person before.

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:08.660
The rumors that they secretly came
to the <i>Tenkaido</i> were true...

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:12.380
Commander Jack and Commander Queen.

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:16.550
Two of the top three Intercept
Faction leaders are together.

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:22.090
As you're aware, the Kill-T-Gangs are attacking more frequently.

00:03:22.430 --> 00:03:26.890
Of course, we in the Intercept Faction
intend to fight them to the end.

00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:30.020
But if we remain on the defensive forever,

00:03:30.020 --> 00:03:33.520
they'll eventually break through
the Impactor defense system.

00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:36.980
Which would mean that the Earth is doomed.

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:43.740
Thus, we are finally initiating our
primary plan, Operation Summer.

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:46.740
Captain, explain the plan.

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:48.200
Yes, ma'am.

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:54.580
Nishikubo doesn't seem to be here.

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:58.090
I heard he was sending someone in his place.

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:00.340
But he's still just a kid.

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:04.930
I'm Manatsu Daichi, of the Midsummer's Knights.

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:09.810
We will destroy the Cocoon, the core of the
Planetary Gears' fortress-class carrier <i>Oberon</i>,

00:04:09.810 --> 00:04:12.140
which is in orbit around Uranus.

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:16.900
That is our counteroffensive plan against
the Kill-T-Gangs: Operation Summer.

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:19.940
So they're the Midsummer's Knights.

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:23.240
The Earth Engine, Nebula Engine, and Flare Engine,

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:27.240
our three manned Impactors, will
be loaded on the spaceship <i>Kivotos</i>,

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:31.200
which will then dock with the <i>Blume</i>,
currently connected to the <i>Tenkaido</i>.

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:36.920
The <i>Blume</i>'s Entangle Link Navigation
enables hyperspace travel.

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:41.550
We'll reach orbit around Uranus a few
hours after the mission begins.

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:47.720
And we'll use the Engine series aboard
the <i>Kivotos</i> to destroy <i>Oberon</i>.

00:04:48.390 --> 00:04:51.470
The Boosted Plazmagnum,
a destructive weapon that will

00:04:51.470 --> 00:04:57.230
completely delete the intelligence information
contained within the Livlasters' Orgone energy

00:04:57.690 --> 00:05:03.190
and convert it to pure energy, will be
loaded onto both the Earth and Nebula.

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:06.950
Alonzo has calculated that this weapon is capable

00:05:06.950 --> 00:05:11.990
of destroying the Cocoon, which forms the
<i>Oberon</i>'s core and holds the Ego Blocks.

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:16.540
Naturally, we'll need to run a test before we attack.

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:20.920
But we can use this to wipe out the Planetary Gears

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:23.010
that have invaded the Solar System.

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:28.390
Captain, I've received a report
that your Livlaster's output

00:05:28.390 --> 00:05:32.770
has surpassed the energy
requirement for this weapon.

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:37.730
But can you replicate that output?

00:05:40.730 --> 00:05:41.440
I think so.

00:05:47.150 --> 00:05:49.870
Can they really handle this?

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:52.330
Nishikubo chose them.

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:55.870
Of course, I believe in him, but...

00:05:56.460 --> 00:06:01.170
The idea is to eliminate the
Kivotos Plan's cold sleep block.

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:06.380
Either way, if the Ark Faction
finds out, we'll have a problem.

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:10.760
How did it feel to be back in space after so long?

00:06:11.180 --> 00:06:13.430
It's hard for an old man...

00:06:13.430 --> 00:06:16.020
Let's leave space to the young ones.

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:19.020
But not just any young ones.

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:20.610
Of course.

00:06:21.110 --> 00:06:23.730
The young men and women who go into space

00:06:23.730 --> 00:06:27.110
must be the chosen ones,
who will carry humanity's fate.

00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:31.490
We cannot let the Intercept Faction
get any further out of control.

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:35.330
It seems they told the public media
that the spaceship <i>Blume</i>,

00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:38.540
which surfaced in the seas around Tanegashima,

00:06:38.540 --> 00:06:42.750
was a secretly developed giant
asteroid defense interceptor.

00:06:42.750 --> 00:06:47.970
All of this just makes it vexing that
we can't tell them the truth...

00:06:48.550 --> 00:06:53.550
The Intercept Faction's leaders are
gathering aboard the <i>Tenkaido</i>.

00:06:53.550 --> 00:06:55.100
There isn't much time.

00:06:55.510 --> 00:06:57.180
I sent Pointer.

00:06:57.680 --> 00:06:58.890
Pointer?

00:06:59.890 --> 00:07:01.400
Will that be all right?

00:07:02.190 --> 00:07:06.280
Pointer is on his way, not as a Salty Dog member,

00:07:06.610 --> 00:07:09.110
but on his own.

00:07:09.990 --> 00:07:12.070
He's perfect for the job.

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:16.040
He hates them more than anyone.

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:19.040
Satellitejack

00:07:22.420 --> 00:07:28.840
The inter-satellite transport ship <i>Nipper</i>
is now arriving from Delta-1, at Dock 14.

00:07:29.340 --> 00:07:31.840
Akari's coming on this ship.

00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:32.640
Are you happy?

00:07:33.140 --> 00:07:34.640
Of course I am.

00:07:35.470 --> 00:07:37.890
Just as happy as I was to see you.

00:07:41.270 --> 00:07:43.100
I hope she gets here soon!

00:08:07.460 --> 00:08:08.300
Akari!

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:11.720
Hana.

00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:20.600
Are you tired?

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:23.140
There was no direct shuttle...

00:08:23.140 --> 00:08:26.560
Coming in via Delta-1 was a
bigger pain than I expected.

00:08:27.150 --> 00:08:28.570
Where are the boys?

00:08:29.190 --> 00:08:31.070
Combat training.

00:08:31.070 --> 00:08:33.650
When I win, the Blue Star is mine!

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:36.820
It won't be that easy, Captain.

00:08:38.660 --> 00:08:41.250
Those two boys are flirting with each other <i>again</i>?

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:43.120
Yup.

00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:46.960
Next, please.

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:12.570
The contacts Salty Dog gave me worked perfectly.

00:09:26.710 --> 00:09:28.040
It's Ai!

00:09:28.040 --> 00:09:33.880
Everyone, the beloved idol Ai is here to be <i>Tenkaido</i>'s

00:09:34.970 --> 00:09:37.220
governor for a day!

00:09:48.900 --> 00:09:50.150
Cheerful!

00:09:50.150 --> 00:09:51.150
Cheerful!

00:09:51.150 --> 00:09:52.690
Pounding!

00:09:52.690 --> 00:09:53.650
Pounding!

00:09:54.320 --> 00:09:56.900
Heart!

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:02.490
Ai!

00:10:03.870 --> 00:10:05.790
Are idols important?

00:10:05.790 --> 00:10:08.620
Almost as important as magical girls.

00:10:18.050 --> 00:10:21.680
So today, for a special summer project,

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:24.770
I've been governor of the <i>Tenkaido</i> for a day.

00:10:25.180 --> 00:10:30.520
Globe just stunned the world when a
giant asteroid defense interceptor

00:10:30.520 --> 00:10:33.270
was launched from Tanegashima.

00:10:33.270 --> 00:10:38.820
Is there anything you can tell me about it?

00:10:39.610 --> 00:10:44.200
How did you get something so large up here?

00:10:44.660 --> 00:10:47.790
We used cutting-edge laser propulsion technology.

00:10:47.790 --> 00:10:51.130
Laser propulsion! Amazing!

00:10:51.130 --> 00:10:55.670
Then, then... The stories saying that
people saw a bright ray of light

00:10:55.670 --> 00:10:57.840
shooting into the night sky in Tanegashima...

00:10:58.170 --> 00:11:01.430
Could those have anything to do with it?

00:11:01.430 --> 00:11:02.340
That's right.

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:05.810
Nonsense.

00:11:05.810 --> 00:11:09.940
This planet can't create a device like
that with its present technology.

00:11:10.810 --> 00:11:13.270
Pac is not the only liar.

00:11:14.230 --> 00:11:16.110
Amara and his friends have moved.

00:11:16.860 --> 00:11:20.820
Yes. They plan to do something on the <i>Tenkaido</i>.

00:11:30.160 --> 00:11:32.960
Now, then... Let's see what happens.

00:11:34.460 --> 00:11:38.840
I'm sorry... A lot of this involves military secrets,

00:11:39.210 --> 00:11:41.550
so I can't tell you any more.

00:11:41.550 --> 00:11:45.300
Thank you for taking the time to talk to me.

00:11:45.300 --> 00:11:48.470
I'm so happy I got a chance to visit this satellite,

00:11:48.970 --> 00:11:55.360
on the frontier of space development, and to
meet all of the wonderful people who work here!

00:11:55.940 --> 00:11:57.150
Okay, everyone...

00:11:57.150 --> 00:11:59.190
I'll see you back on Earth!

00:12:01.530 --> 00:12:02.990
And cut.

00:12:05.870 --> 00:12:07.330
Thank you.

00:12:07.330 --> 00:12:08.660
Thank you.

00:12:08.660 --> 00:12:10.540
Thank you, Ai—

00:12:11.710 --> 00:12:13.120
I mean, Miss Ai.

00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:17.460
Thank you.

00:12:18.170 --> 00:12:20.300
You can call me Ai.

00:12:20.300 --> 00:12:22.420
But it really was fun.

00:12:22.420 --> 00:12:24.720
It's my first time in space.

00:12:25.090 --> 00:12:26.930
Ai, for the rest of your time here,

00:12:26.930 --> 00:12:29.220
we'll show you around the <i>Tenkaido</i>.

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:31.020
I hope you enjoy it.

00:12:31.020 --> 00:12:32.640
Okay, thanks.

00:12:33.980 --> 00:12:36.980
How can you win without blocking?

00:12:36.980 --> 00:12:39.400
I guess I've been doing this longer than you.

00:12:39.780 --> 00:12:43.070
If you can do it, so can I.

00:12:44.610 --> 00:12:47.200
I love the way you never give up.

00:12:49.330 --> 00:12:51.620
Good job today!

00:12:53.580 --> 00:12:57.460
Wow! A pool in space!

00:12:57.920 --> 00:13:00.090
There's nothing special about a pool.

00:13:00.090 --> 00:13:04.050
I think this is my first time visiting
a pool outside of photo shoots.

00:13:04.050 --> 00:13:05.760
I see...

00:13:05.760 --> 00:13:09.510
Your job doesn't allow you a lot of
freedom in your private life, huh?

00:13:09.510 --> 00:13:10.680
Do you have a boyfriend?

00:13:10.680 --> 00:13:13.140
You can't ask that.

00:13:13.140 --> 00:13:16.440
I don't have many friends...

00:13:17.060 --> 00:13:20.400
When I go out, I have to worry
about people watching me.

00:13:20.400 --> 00:13:23.860
Truthfully, I think I'm hard to hang out with.

00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:29.120
But here, you don't have to
worry about other people!

00:13:29.120 --> 00:13:33.160
Unfortunately, there aren't
many boys our age around.

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:46.050
That's Manatsu Daichi and Arashi Teppei.

00:13:47.090 --> 00:13:48.800
They're boys our age!

00:13:49.470 --> 00:13:51.510
I'm Ai. Hello, there.

00:13:52.510 --> 00:13:53.720
Hello.

00:13:53.720 --> 00:13:56.850
I think this is my first time talking to a celebrity.

00:13:56.850 --> 00:13:58.770
He's more into trends than I thought?

00:13:58.770 --> 00:14:00.110
Trends?

00:14:09.530 --> 00:14:12.120
And he's totally unaffected...

00:14:14.950 --> 00:14:17.500
Both commanders seemed concerned.

00:14:18.080 --> 00:14:20.710
As am I, frankly.

00:14:21.500 --> 00:14:23.710
Akari is still a child.

00:14:24.300 --> 00:14:26.420
Do you really think this is okay?

00:14:26.420 --> 00:14:28.130
She's an adult.

00:14:28.630 --> 00:14:31.800
Since she joined Globe, I've learned that well.

00:14:32.260 --> 00:14:36.060
Manatsu Daichi still looks like a child to me, as well.

00:14:36.770 --> 00:14:41.190
And yet, we have to leave him in
charge of such a major operation.

00:14:42.190 --> 00:14:44.150
Daichi will do it.

00:14:44.860 --> 00:14:46.320
I'm confident in that.

00:14:47.280 --> 00:14:51.370
When I first heard the reports about
Mutou Hana and Arashi Teppei,

00:14:51.370 --> 00:14:52.780
I was really surprised.

00:14:53.410 --> 00:14:57.040
I wondered why you'd allow such
dangerous elements on your team.

00:14:57.450 --> 00:15:01.880
I heard you told Hana you'd be her mother.

00:15:03.420 --> 00:15:05.300
If she becomes my daughter,

00:15:05.300 --> 00:15:08.670
she can obtain the rights of an
Earthling and a Japanese citizenship.

00:15:09.340 --> 00:15:14.350
Once the operation is over,
I can give her a place to come home to...

00:15:15.140 --> 00:15:16.470
Why did you think of that?

00:15:17.520 --> 00:15:18.680
Why?

00:15:18.680 --> 00:15:21.850
The reason you wanted to make
her your daughter was because,

00:15:21.850 --> 00:15:24.650
after meeting her, your intuition told you to, right?

00:15:28.150 --> 00:15:32.570
Do you remember the shot bar where we first met?

00:15:32.570 --> 00:15:34.450
What are you talking about?

00:15:34.450 --> 00:15:36.330
You mean that one in Daikanyama?

00:15:36.950 --> 00:15:39.540
I don't normally do things like that...

00:15:39.540 --> 00:15:42.710
But despite never having seen you
before, I talked to you that day.

00:15:43.540 --> 00:15:46.670
For some reason, I felt like I had to do it.

00:15:48.380 --> 00:15:53.010
We've split up now, but I still consider
myself lucky to have met you.

00:15:54.220 --> 00:15:59.520
I think my intuition was right in
telling me to talk to you that day.

00:16:00.850 --> 00:16:05.900
Ultimately, I think that's the only way
humans can judge what's truly important.

00:16:07.320 --> 00:16:11.780
I want to believe in my intuition and yours.

00:16:12.990 --> 00:16:17.490
Even so, Arashi Teppei is an enemy
avatar and retains his memories as such.

00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:21.210
To be honest, I don't understand him.

00:16:24.790 --> 00:16:27.420
Teppei isn't dangerous.

00:16:28.340 --> 00:16:34.720
He's an indispensable member
of the Midsummer's Knights.

00:16:36.800 --> 00:16:38.640
Did you talk to them about the Planter Unit?

00:16:39.470 --> 00:16:42.640
They're doing their best, but there's no time.

00:16:43.270 --> 00:16:43.940
I see.

00:16:45.060 --> 00:16:50.150
But why would they send an idol as a
governor for a day at a time like this?

00:16:50.150 --> 00:16:52.950
The PR department came up with the idea.

00:16:52.950 --> 00:16:54.570
I took advantage of it.

00:16:55.070 --> 00:16:57.370
It's a good feint for the real operation.

00:16:58.240 --> 00:17:04.580
The Ark Faction can't do anything crazy
with an idol aboard? Was that it?

00:17:06.000 --> 00:17:07.330
I hope you're right.

00:17:08.670 --> 00:17:09.840
We're on schedule.

00:17:10.750 --> 00:17:12.260
Got it.

00:17:22.640 --> 00:17:23.890
Working hard, guys?

00:17:25.980 --> 00:17:28.110
Hi, Ai!

00:17:29.980 --> 00:17:32.570
She really is cute...

00:17:41.620 --> 00:17:43.410
Time to get to work.

00:17:54.340 --> 00:17:55.840
Cheerful...

00:17:55.840 --> 00:17:57.430
Starving...

00:17:57.430 --> 00:17:58.930
Vampire!

00:18:03.220 --> 00:18:05.390
The <i>Kivotos</i> spaceship holds the people

00:18:06.060 --> 00:18:08.900
who were entrusted with humanity's future.

00:18:11.020 --> 00:18:12.570
We'll send them back to Earth,

00:18:13.230 --> 00:18:18.280
and use the spaceship they were
going to use to execute our mission.

00:18:19.410 --> 00:18:23.790
But aren't you also fighting for them, Captain?

00:18:24.910 --> 00:18:27.580
You'll save the people sleeping inside here too, right?

00:18:28.920 --> 00:18:29.500
Yeah.

00:18:33.800 --> 00:18:34.920
Hey, Teppei...

00:18:36.590 --> 00:18:40.180
Is it still hard for you to have fun with everyone?

00:18:41.720 --> 00:18:47.270
I mean, I'm the type who prefers to be alone, as well.

00:18:48.140 --> 00:18:50.690
I don't think you understand.

00:18:50.690 --> 00:18:51.730
What do you mean?

00:18:52.440 --> 00:18:57.110
I don't think anyone really understands me.

00:18:57.650 --> 00:19:03.700
Hana is like me, a life form born
outside this solar system.

00:19:04.490 --> 00:19:08.210
However, Hana may have been born like me,

00:19:08.910 --> 00:19:12.420
but her mentality is much
closer to yours than to mine.

00:19:13.630 --> 00:19:17.170
When I get close to a girl,
what am I supposed to do?

00:19:18.050 --> 00:19:21.510
I have a telepathic kiss like Hana.

00:19:21.840 --> 00:19:25.100
But my experiences and memories are vast.

00:19:25.100 --> 00:19:29.020
They're beyond Earth humans' comprehension.

00:19:29.730 --> 00:19:34.610
The information shared in a short kiss
is only the surface thoughts.

00:19:35.690 --> 00:19:40.610
But if I kissed someone deeply,
and they touched the other parts,

00:19:41.610 --> 00:19:44.870
who knows what darkness would swallow them?

00:19:46.240 --> 00:19:49.580
Memories of thousands, tens of thousands of years.

00:19:51.080 --> 00:19:56.550
The time I spend with Daichi,
Hana, and you is truly enjoyable.

00:19:57.420 --> 00:20:01.840
But sometimes, in the middle of it,
it's as if I return to myself.

00:20:01.840 --> 00:20:06.560
It suddenly feels like everything
is a dream with no substance.

00:20:07.760 --> 00:20:10.230
"What is this I'm looking at?"

00:20:10.850 --> 00:20:13.230
"Is it truly real, and not just a dream?"

00:20:13.690 --> 00:20:16.940
"After thousands, tens of thousands of years,

00:20:16.940 --> 00:20:20.190
what is this I find when I meet you?"

00:20:20.690 --> 00:20:22.150
"What am I?"

00:20:22.150 --> 00:20:26.620
"Why did I cross this vast gulf of
time and space to come here?"

00:20:26.620 --> 00:20:29.830
"If there is a meaning, what is it?!"

00:20:34.080 --> 00:20:37.960
Sometimes, I feel as if thoughts
like these are about to crush me.

00:20:41.840 --> 00:20:46.300
Does this mean you've finally turned to me for help?

00:20:48.930 --> 00:20:50.060
I...

00:20:51.220 --> 00:20:56.690
I know why you're here right now.

00:20:59.320 --> 00:21:00.610
Teppei...

00:21:02.150 --> 00:21:06.070
The reason you're here with me right now

00:21:06.910 --> 00:21:14.160
is that my god crossed vast gulfs of
space and time to lead you here.

00:21:41.110 --> 00:21:41.690
What?

00:21:42.110 --> 00:21:46.740
People of the <i>Tenkaido</i>, I'd like your attention.

00:21:46.740 --> 00:21:52.540
I've learned of the Globe Intercept
Faction's Operation Summer,

00:21:53.160 --> 00:21:58.750
and have come to stop these ideas
that threaten to destroy humanity.

00:21:58.750 --> 00:22:02.460
The <i>Tenkaido</i> will temporarily
remain under my control.

00:22:03.300 --> 00:22:06.970
I will now take action to stop Operation Summer.

00:22:07.470 --> 00:22:10.180
But I'd like you to know that
my actions are entirely due

00:22:10.640 --> 00:22:13.270
to my personal desire for all
humanity's continued prosperity,

00:22:13.600 --> 00:22:19.190
and that I am not part of any
organization at this time.

00:22:19.850 --> 00:22:23.400
Hey, this is getting interesting!

00:22:24.230 --> 00:22:27.860
That voice... Hirose, from Salty Dog?

00:22:33.030 --> 00:22:37.120
It's been a long time, kid.

00:22:39.080 --> 00:22:41.330
I'm taking Hana back.

00:24:13.010 --> 00:24:15.680
Salty Dog's Hirose has taken over the <i>Tenkaido</i>.

00:24:15.680 --> 00:24:19.310
And now, the <i>Tenkaido</i> is in even more trouble!

00:24:19.310 --> 00:24:21.640
Countless bits of debris in the satellite's orbit

00:24:21.640 --> 00:24:24.100
begin to attack the <i>Tenkaido</i>.

00:24:24.650 --> 00:24:27.320
This is an attack by the Planetary Gears!

00:24:27.320 --> 00:24:28.110
What do we do?

00:24:28.110 --> 00:24:30.280
Can we stop them?

00:24:30.280 --> 00:24:33.820
Next time, on episode 21 of <i>Captain Earth</i>:

00:24:33.820 --> 00:24:35.570
The Meaning of a Captain

00:24:34.280 --> 00:24:35.570
The Meaning of a Captain.

00:24:35.870 --> 00:24:38.080
Earth Engine, expand!
